.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_EVENT_SET 9S
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_event_set ,
.Nm ndi_event_set_t
.Nd set of nexus event definitions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An \fBndi_event_set_t\fP groups event definitions for binding to or unbinding
from a nexus event handle.
Initialize all members before passing the structure to the event framework.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va ndi_events_version
Set to \fBNDI_EVENTS_REV1\fP.
The older value \fBNDI_EVENTS_REV0\fP is not accepted by the current framework.
.It Va ndi_n_events
Number of entries in \fBndi_event_defs\fP, representable as a \fBushort_t\fP.
.It Va ndi_event_defs
Pointer to an array of \fBndi_event_definition_t\fP structures.
The array and referenced name strings must remain valid while bound.
The set descriptor itself need only remain valid for the bind or unbind call.
.El
.Pp
Multiple sets can be bound to one handle, subject to event-name and execution
level restrictions.
An unbind set may name a subset of the bound events.
Remove all callbacks for those events before unbinding.
.Sh STRUCTURE MEMBERS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ushort_t                ndi_events_version;
ushort_t                ndi_n_events;
ndi_event_definition_t  *ndi_event_defs;
.Ed
.Sh EXAMPLES
Define a kernel-context event with targeted delivery:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static ndi_event_definition_t events[] = {
        { 0, "example:device-change", EPL_KERNEL,
            NDI_EVENT_POST_TO_TGT }
};
.Pp
static ndi_event_set_t event_set = {
        NDI_EVENTS_REV1,
        sizeof (events) / sizeof (events[0]),
        events
};
.Ed
Bind the set during nexus attachment using \fBndi_event_bind_set()\fP.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_event_alloc_hdl 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_definition 9S
